          "date": "2026-09-25 15:56:57.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-17768 build: embed BTF in Lustre kernel modules",
        "message": "LU-17768 build: embed BTF in Lustre kernel modules\n\nOut-of-tree modules lack .BTF sections because kbuild's\nMakefile.modfinal skips BTF generation without\n$(objtree)/vmlinux, which kernel-devel does not ship.\n\nAdd config/embed-btf.sh and run it from the modules make\ntarget after kbuild.  pahole encodes a distilled base\n(.BTF.base) so the module BTF relocates against the running\nkernel at load time.\n\nThe base BTF must come from the kernel the modules are built\nagainst, not the running kernel: take $(LINUX_OBJ)/vmlinux\nwhen the build tree has one (custom-built kernels; the same\nsource kbuild itself uses), else /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux only\nwhen building against the running kernel.  Otherwise skip\nembedding, since BTF encoded against a foreign base fails\nbtf_relocate() at load time, and with\nCONFIG_MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH=n that makes the module\nunloadable.  The earlier commit b5c451820443 (\"LU-17768 build:\nembed BTF in Lustre kernel modules\") always used\n/sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux, so modules built against a kernel\nother than the running one would not load, and it was reverted.\n\nEncoding is best effort: a module pahole cannot encode keeps\nno BTF rather than failing the build.\n\nGated at configure time on CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES\n(kernel 5.9+).\n\nKeep both .BTF and .BTF.base through find-debuginfo so\nthey reach the shipped RPMs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Sohei Koyama <skoyama@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I038ebf6aa3d183b43c72c409ea1a88b70e06aab6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
